WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:06.779
Speaker 1: Folks, it looks to me that California
Governor Gavin Newsom is running for president

00:00:06.779 --> 00:00:08.120
in 2024.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:13.980
California Governor Gavin Newsom was interviewed
by Fox, L.A. and Gavin Newsom comes out swinging

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:19.180
and points out exactly what I've been saying
about Democrats for a decade now.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.440
Gavin Newsom says We shouldn't be playing
defense.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.770
We should be playing offense.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:26.920
Democrats must be ferocious.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.840
Democrats must be ruthless.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.719
This is exactly what I have been saying for
over a decade on this program.

00:00:32.719 --> 00:00:40.329
I am not saying that Gavin Newsom is my preferred
politician, that I agree with him on every

00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:42.750
issue that is the epitome of a progressive.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:51.519
But this guy identifies the exact issue is
using the right language, is pointing out

00:00:51.519 --> 00:00:54.050
exactly what I've been pointing out.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.920
He's coming out swinging.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.929
Take a look at this from his interview over
the weekend.

00:00:57.929 --> 00:01:02.079
Speaker 2: You have to also recognize what
you're up against.

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:06.260
And right now, we're up against the ruthlessness
of a Republican Party.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.460
And I say that not naively.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.460
I don't say that.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.720
I'm not just not a cheap shot.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:16.710
You see what's happening to all the progress
we've made in the 21st century, all of the

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.700
rights that we in many ways have taken for
granted that have been afforded since the

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.840
sixties are being rolled back in real time.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.960
This is a totally different moment, and we
have to wake up with a different mindset and

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:32.400
not just old mindset in terms of just a collaborative
mindset, a cup of tea, and everyone's going

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.750
to work together to get along.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:37.310
Think ways to advance the collective cause.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.070
And that's where the party needs to come in.

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:46.340
Democrats need the Democratic Party, not the
president, not a speaker, not an elected office.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:47.680
Speaker 1: All right, guys.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.840
He's pointing out the absurdity of thinking
you're going to have a cup of tea with the

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.020
modern Republican Party and figure things
out and hash things out with them.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.440
He is exactly correct.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:02.800
Speaker 2: The party, the infrastructure,
I think, has to organize with more ferocity

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:09.580
of focus, more determination to set the agenda,
set the course, and put the other party on

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:10.580
the defensive.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:12.160
They are dominating the narrative.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.540
The facts aren't on their side, but they're
dominating there.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.200
And in this world right now, you dominate
the narrative.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.200
You win.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.920
And that's what I'm worried about and that's
what I'm expressing.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.220
Speaker 1: So this is all part of his gubernatorial
campaign for reelection.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:28.350
But he is doing a lot of different things
that suggest greater ambitions.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:32.120
He is running ads in Florida saying, hey,
if you want to come to the place with real

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.840
freedom, leave Florida, come to California.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:40.200
He's doing interviews in which he is addressing
the major issues facing structurally from

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.660
a PR perspective, from a messaging perspective,
facing the Democratic Party.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.319
I'm not endorsing Gavin Newsom.

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:46.319
He's not even running.

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:47.900
He's not the most progressive.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:53.260
But this is a guy who could be president now
if he ran the smear campaign would be brutal,

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.840
but it would also be pretty toothless.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:55.840
I mean, okay.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.000
Stuff about his dating history.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:01.010
You know, he was once married to kimberly
guilfoyle now who is now married to Donald

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:02.010
Trump Jr.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.010
That's weird.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:06.991
That doesn't that that's you know, it makes
it makes me question someone's choices, that's

00:03:06.991 --> 00:03:07.991
for sure.

00:03:07.991 --> 00:03:12.610
He had this dinner at the expensive restaurant,
the French Laundry, during COVID, when you

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:13.680
weren't supposed to be doing that.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:14.680
That was wrong.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:16.980
And he's going to get he's going to get hit
with that.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:22.760
But they are potentially going to expose themselves
if they have to run against Newsom, because

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:27.849
from what's known, at least right now, the
criticisms and attacks on him would be brutal

00:03:27.849 --> 00:03:29.700
but also quite toothless.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.200
And Gavin Newsom is 100% correct here.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.780
They have to be playing defense.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:36.930
They're the ones who are out of step with
the views of the American people.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:39.620
Why is it that the left is constantly playing
defense?

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:44.840
They are the ones who are proposing policy
that would be disastrous for millions of Americans,

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:48.390
whether it's on health care, whether it's
getting rid of Roe v Wade, whatever the case

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:49.480
is.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:54.170
He's getting it and he is speaking about it
in a way that I'm not really hearing anybody

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:56.040
else talk about it right now.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:59.599
So not endorsing anyone.

00:03:59.599 --> 00:04:03.880
It's very interesting that he has got this
messaging down pat because this is the right

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:04.880
messaging.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:08.819
And by the way, this messaging is much more
relevant on the national stage when you think,

00:04:08.819 --> 00:04:09.819
okay, California.

00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:15.570
California has large geographic areas that
are conservative, but from a population standpoint,

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:17.380
California is not conservative.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:22.280
And when he talks about the strategy and tactics
that are required against this Republican

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:27.160
Party, it's fine to keep it in mind if you're
running for governor in California, but really

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.160
it's relevant nationally.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.750
So this is super interesting.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:33.380
We'll have this interview on our Instagram
at David Pakman show.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:34.490
Check it out.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:35.490
Tell me what you think.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:05:02.370
I'm liking what 

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:48.210
I'm hearing

